Lyman-alpha wing opacity induced by collisions H-H2.                            
This is based on quasi-static theory and includes Doppler broadening.           
The cross section sigma[cm^2] was given in the form: LOG_10 (sigma)
per emitter per perturber [cm^5]!
D.K. obtained from http://www.icate-conicet.gob.ar/rohrmann/tables.html         
sigma was multiplied by 88.53e-30**1215.671)**2 to transform the cross
section to a line profile, and additionally by e18 for numerical reasons.
This is reversed in the code by eta(n,l).
The normalization in profdata is like the other Balmer lines by multiplying
with perturber density/e18. D.K. fecit 20200528.
    7  number of tables
    21.00 perturber density  nH2
    8 number of temperatures 
